<!-- livebook:{"persist_outputs":true} -->

# STAC API Examples with Req

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:req, "~> 0.5"}
])
```

## Setup

Configure the STAC API base URL and the two static keys. Point `STAC_BASE_URL` at another
deployment to run the read-only parts against it; the write examples are meant for a local
dev server.

```elixir
base_url = System.get_env("STAC_BASE_URL") || "https://metadata.geokuup.ee" # "http://localhost:4000"
api_version = "/stac/api/v1"
manage_version = "/stac/manage/v1"

# The two static keys from the server config (STAC_API_KEY / STAC_API_KEY_RO).
# STAC_API_KEY is the admin key: the only one that can manage personal API keys.
read_write_api_key = System.get_env("LB_STAC_API_KEY_RW") || "dev-api-key-2024"
read_only_api_key = System.get_env("LB_STAC_API_KEY_RO") || "dev-read-only-key-2024"

# STAC API read client: public endpoints, no auth required.
# Add an X-API-Key header to unlock private catalogs, collections and items.
req = Req.new(base_url: base_url <> api_version)

# Management API client: all CRUD needs a read-write key.
manage_req =
  Req.new(
    base_url: base_url <> manage_version,
    headers: [{"x-api-key", read_write_api_key}]
  )

%{stac_api: base_url <> api_version, manage_api: base_url <> manage_version}
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{
  stac_api: "https://metadata.geokuup.ee/stac/api/v1",
  manage_api: "https://metadata.geokuup.ee/stac/manage/v1"
}
```

## Example 1: Exploring the API

Catalogs are listed through the Management API (`/stac/manage/v1`), which always needs a
read-write key. Collections and items are also readable through the public STAC API
(`/stac/api/v1`).

```elixir
# Root landing page: conformance classes and links
{:ok, response} = Req.get(req, url: "/")

IO.puts("Status: #{response.status}")
IO.puts("Title: #{response.body["title"]}")
IO.puts("conformsTo: #{length(response.body["conformsTo"])} classes")

Enum.map(response.body["links"], &{&1["rel"], &1["href"]})
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
Status: 200
Title: Geokuup STAC API
conformsTo: 9 classes
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

