## Example 2: Creating Resources (With Auth)

Creating, updating and deleting go through the Management API with a read-write
`X-API-Key`. Use `manage_req` from Setup.

Write responses are wrapped in `success` / `message` / `data`. Besides the STAC fields
they carry `created` / `updated` (RFC 3339, UTC), and collections carry `catalog_id`.

### Create a Root Catalog

```elixir
catalog_data = %{
  "id" => "my-test-catalog",
  "title" => "My Test Catalog",
  "description" => "A catalog for testing purposes",
  "type" => "Catalog",
  "stac_version" => "1.0.0",
  "links" => [
    %{
      "rel" => "license",
      "href" => "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
      "title" => "CC BY 4.0"
    }
  ]
}

{:ok, response} = Req.post(manage_req, url: "/catalogs", json: catalog_data)

# 201 on the first run, 409 if the catalog already exists
IO.puts("Status: #{response.status}")
response.body
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
Status: 201
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{
  "data" => %{
    "created" => "2026-11-16T15:57:52.911070Z",
    "description" => "A catalog for testing purposes",
    "extent" => nil,
    "id" => "my-test-catalog",
    "links" => [
      %{
        "href" => "https://metadata.geokuup.ee/stac/api/v1/catalog/my-test-catalog",
        "rel" => "self",
        "type" => "application/json"
