### Issue a read-write key with an expiry date

Typical for a student or project key that should end with the semester. `expires_at`
must lie in the future and carry an offset (`Z` or `+02:00`).

```elixir
end_of_semester =
  DateTime.utc_now() |> DateTime.add(90 * 86_400, :second) |> DateTime.truncate(:second)

{:ok, response} =
  Req.post(manage_req,
    url: "/api-keys",
    json: %{
      "name" => "Upload script #{suffix}",
      "role" => "read_write",
      "expires_at" => DateTime.to_iso8601(end_of_semester),
      "contact" => "student@example.org",
      "note" => "Nightly item upload, until the end of the semester"
    }
  )

IO.puts("Status: #{response.status}")

rw_key = response.body["data"]["key"]
rw_key_id = response.body["data"]["id"]

Map.update!(response.body["data"], "key", mask)
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
Status: 201
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{
  "contact" => "student@example.org",
  "expires_at" => "2027-02-14T15:45:03.000000Z",
  "id" => 10,
  "inserted_at" => "2026-11-16T15:45:03.044708Z",
  "key" => "stac_rw_jnOf…",
  "key_prefix" => "stac_rw_jnOf",
  "last_used_at" => nil,
  "name" => "Upload script 6594",
  "note" => "Nightly item upload, until the end of the semester",
  "role" => "read_write",
  "updated_at" => "2026-11-16T15:45:03.044708Z"
}
```

### List and show keys

Listing never returns secrets, only the `key_prefix`. `last_used_at` is `null` until a key
is used and is updated at most once an hour.

```elixir
{:ok, response} = Req.get(manage_req, url: "/api-keys")

IO.puts("Status: #{response.status}")

response.body["data"]
|> Enum.filter(&String.ends_with?(&1["name"], "#{suffix}"))
|> Enum.map(&Map.take(&1, ["id", "name", "role", "key_prefix", "expires_at", "last_used_at"]))
```

